    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::3716545345",
      "Source": "ARK: Fantastic Tames - Season 1",
      "Trans": {"SC":"方舟：奇幻驯兽 - 第一季","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::3857148935",
      "Source": "Common name:\r\nAraneo\r\nSpecies: Araneomorphus Amalgotantibus\r\nTime: Seemingly Recent\r\nDiet: Carnivore\r\nTemperament: Opportunistic, Aggressive\r\n\r\nWild\r\nLately I’ve noticed a kind of breakthrough evolution in the local population of Araneomorphus. Broodmother's ‘children’ have suddenly exploded in number, and they've also begun using their amazing amalgam of arachnidial abilities in alarming new ways.\r\n\r\nThese overgrown spiders have begun traversing high areas with their web-lines, and rappelling down them to ambush prey. They also shoot their webbing with a newly ruthless precision--a disorienting innovation that restricts their prey's ability to move, attack, and protect itself. Struck enough times, an entangled victim is as good as helpless.\r\n\r\nDomesticated\r\nThough the Araneo was once considered too small to be a serviceable mount, newer compact saddle designs have turned around opinion. Its narcotic venom turns out to be useful for tranquilizing potential tames. One popular tactic is to drop from above and wrap up a target creature in webbing before subduing them with a venomous bite.\r\n\r\nEven if a taming attempt fails, your spider-mount can harvest the hardened silk from a downed target for a variety of uses. Araneo silk is an excellent insulator in warm-weather clothing, for example.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"通用名称: 虚形蛛\r\n拉丁学名: 混魇虚形蛛\r\n时代: 疑为近代\r\n食性: 肉食\r\n性情: 机会主义性好战\r\n\r\n\r\n野生\r\n近日, 我注意到混魇虚形蛛的本土种群存在某种突破性的演化。最令人担心的不仅是这群育母蜘蛛的“子嗣”数量骤增, 而且这些蜘蛛也开始以令人不安的新方式, 运用它们那套混杂而惊人的蛛类能力。\r\n这些庞大的蜘蛛可以通过蛛丝穿行于高低错落的地形, 并迅速索降, 突袭猎物; 此外, 它们还能以精进的精确度无情的喷吐蜘蛛网 —— 这种进步的蛛网可以令目标迷失方向, 并极大地限制其行动、攻击和自卫能力。而一旦目标被多次击中, 被缠住的目标便只能任其宰割了。\r\n\r\n\r\n家养\r\n虽然过去认为虚形蛛体型相对人比较小, 不适合骑乘, 但新型紧凑的鞍具设计推翻了这一认知。其具有昏迷效果的毒液, 在麻醉驯服目标生物时也大有可为。主流的策略通常是骑乘虚形蛛从目标上方快速索降, 喷吐蛛丝, 束缚目标生物, 在注射毒液将其击晕。\r\n即便驯服失手, 虚形蛛也能从死亡的目标身上采集硬化蛛丝, 蛛丝作为一种上好的隔热材料, 用途十分广泛。例如可制作在温暖气候行动时的护具。","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::3651805070",
      "Source": "Common name:\r\nStegosaurus\r\nSpecies: Stegosaurus regium\r\nTime: Late Jurassic\r\nDiet: Herbivore\r\nTemperament: Docile\r\n\r\nWild\r\nStegosaurus regium has approximately 16 paired rows of plates along its back, flanked by another, smaller pair of 6 plates. This is contrary to the alternating rows of Stegosaurus fossils I've seen in museums. I've encountered Stegosaurus, in varying amounts, almost everywhere on the Island.\r\n\r\nNot surprisingly, Stegosaurus uses the spines on its tail to defend itself. While not aggressive, Stegosaurus will come to the aid of another nearby Stegosaurus. This implies it to be a herd animal. \r\n\r\nDomesticated\r\nStegosaurus is commonly used as a safe way to transport large quantities of goods. The plates on its back double as a cover against the arrows of attackers. It is capable of knocking back enemies with its large swinging tail, keeping the predator at a distance long enough for the rest of the tribe to provide backup. Its spiked appendage also helps it gather wild berries in large quantities.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"通用名称: 剑龙\r\n拉丁学名: Stegosaurus regium\r\n正式名称: 反弹甲剑龙\r\n时代: 晚侏罗世\r\n食性: 植食\r\n性情: 温顺\r\n\r\n\r\n野生\r\n这种剑龙的背上有大约16对板片, 它们侧面还有6对较小的板片。这跟博物馆里剑龙化石的交错板片排布不同。我在岛上几乎所有地方都遇到过不同数量的剑龙。\r\n剑龙理所当然会使用尾巴上的刺来保护自己。虽然剑龙并不好战, 但它会协助周围其他的剑龙, 这暗示了它是一种群居动物。\r\n\r\n\r\n家养\r\n剑龙通常被用来安全的传输大量货物。剑龙背上两侧的板片可以防护攻击者的弓箭。它甩尾击退敌人的能力能把掠食者保持在一个足够让部落剩下的成员反击的范围内。同时剑龙的尾部攻击很适合收集大量树果。","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::3576863352",
      "Source": "Species: Antilolexus saxatilis\r\nTime: Unknown\r\nDiet: Herbivore\r\nTemperament: Aggressively Evasive\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWild\r\n\r\nThe latest chimeric creature to cross my path is this figment of Twentieth Century North American folklore -- let’s call it a Burrowbuck (or Burrowdoe). Fantastical as it seems, this horned hare is still a prey species desperate to avoid predation. A startled Burrowbuck will kick up a faceful of blinding dirt as it tunnels away underground.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDomesticated\r\n\r\nA tame Burrowbuck will let you into its surprisingly spacious hidey-holes. While useful as a temporary bunker, its warrens will soon collapse without regular maintenance. You’ll also be rewarded with a handy new travel-network that affords swift movement from entrance to exit... provided a traveler fits through those tight tunnels (sorry, Rexes!). \r\n\r\nAt no extra cost, your furry friend can also dig false entrances to discourage interlopers… Any predator or enemy that tries to enter a Burrowbuck tunnel uninvited risks dropping down a diversionary pitfall instead, that will cave in and trap them.\r\n\r\nBefriending a Burrowbuck just takes a bit of patience. Offer up tasty snacks, and try not to take it personally when you’re wiping grit from your eyes the first few times this clever cryptid skedaddles away. Just remind yourself that their trust is worth digging in to earn..",
      "Trans": {"SC":"通用名称: 穴角兔\r\n拉丁学名: Antilolexus saxatilis\r\n正式名称: 穴栖羚角兔\r\n时代: 时代：未知\r\n食性: 植食\r\n性情: 性情：攻击性回避\r\n\r\n\r\n野生\r\n最近与我擦肩而过的嵌合生物, 竟像是二十世纪北美民俗里凭空跳出来的幻影 —— 就叫它穴角兔吧。它看似荒诞离奇, 却终究仍是一种拼命逃避捕食的猎物。受惊的穴角兔会扬起一脸令人失明的泥土, 随即钻入地下逃之夭夭。\r\n\r\n\r\n家养\r\n驯服后的穴角兔会允许你进入它那出乎意料宽敞的藏身洞。它的洞穴可作为临时地堡使用, 但若不定期维护, 地道很快就会塌陷。你还会获得一套便利的旅行网络, 能让你从入口迅速抵达出口...前提是旅人能挤过那些狭窄地道 (抱歉了, 霸王龙!)。\r\n此外, 你这位毛茸茸的朋友还能免费挖出假入口, 用来劝退不速之客...任何捕食者或敌人若想擅闯穴角兔地道, 都可能一脚跌进诱导陷坑, 被坍塌的土层困在里面。\r\n想与穴角兔交好, 只需要一点耐心。递上美味点心吧；前几次这只机灵的神秘小兽扬起尘土溜之大吉、害你满眼砂砾时, 也别太往心里去。只要记住：它们的信任, 值得你一点点挖出来。","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
