    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::872370676",
      "Source": "Common Name: Helicoprion\r\nSpecies: Helicoprion Frendo\r\nTime: Early Permian \r\nDiet: Soft bodied prey\r\nTemperament: Relaxed\r\n\r\nWild \r\nSimilar in size to Megaladon but far more calm, Helicoprion reclusively lurk in the open waters of the Arks ocean environments. While they are imposing with their familiar silhouette, Helicoprion pose no threat unless provvoked. That is, unless you happen to be an unfortunate ammonite, which Helicoprion have a strong desire to chomp down on!\r\n\r\nWith strong jaws and an evven stronger tail, Helicoprion can pose a dangerous threat if they'e been bothered. The jaws of Helicoprion are used to quickly and efficiently slice up the soft bodies of cephalopod creatures, and the tail in particular has evolvved to be more like a Thresher sharks. This significant change is used to great effect at stunning prey. Some survviving claim more powerful Heli can evven knock out foes with a powerful whip of their tail!\r\n\r\nDomesticated\r\nThe truly remarkable jaw of Helicoprion can be used for much more than just eating Ammonites. Oddly enough, the precise cutting power the tooth whorl provvides can be used to seperate the various components of equipment. For some older specimens, this process allows survivors to record the crafting requirements for their various equipment. I've only seen the most experienced crafters employ this bizarre utility, but it's an astonishingly useful one for sure!",
      "Trans": {"SC":"通用名称: 旋齿鲨\r\n拉丁学名: Helicoprion Frendo\r\n正式名称: 粉碎旋齿鲨\r\n时代: 早二叠世 \r\n食性: 软体动物\r\n性情: 随和\r\n\r\n野生 \r\nSimilar in size to Megaladon but far more calm, Helicoprion reclusively lurk in the open waters of the Arks ocean environments. While they are imposing with their familiar silhouette, Helicoprion pose no threat unless provvoked. That is, unless you happen to be an unfortunate ammonite, which Helicoprion have a strong desire to chomp down on!\r\n\r\nWith strong jaws and an evven stronger tail, Helicoprion can pose a dangerous threat if they'e been bothered. The jaws of Helicoprion are used to quickly and efficiently slice up the soft bodies of cephalopod creatures, and the tail in particular has evolvved to be more like a Thresher sharks. This significant change is used to great effect at stunning prey. Some survviving claim more powerful Heli can evven knock out foes with a powerful whip of their tail!\r\n\r\n家养\r\nThe truly remarkable jaw of Helicoprion can be used for much more than just eating Ammonites. Oddly enough, the precise cutting power the tooth whorl provvides can be used to seperate the various components of equipment. For some older specimens, this process allows survivors to record the crafting requirements for their various equipment. I've only seen the most experienced crafters employ this bizarre utility, but it's an astonishingly useful one for sure!","JA":""},
      //粉碎或磨碎, 粉碎感觉更有冲击力和霸气.
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
