      //模组页面
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "CC3B3CD0481A22A449E22D9F47B28C3F",
      "Source": "Dear Jane,\r\nYou’re probably not gonna be seeing me around the Fourth of July picnic after all. Sure wish I’d gotten around to writing before now, cause I doubt there’s mail service home from wherever it is I’ve found myself. Some tropical island in god-knows-where.\r\nThat’s not me trying to keep secrets. I figure you must’ve heard by now that I never made it ashore in Normandy anyway. Nope, no Ratzis here. But just about everyone and everything else is trying its damnedest to kill me.\r\nGet this: there are living, breathing DINOSAURS on this island. I can guess what you must be thinking right about now: Bobby’s gone clear off his rocker. But I’m writing you hand-on-heart, swear-on-my-dear-Momma’s-grave -- somehow those things are still walking around here, just as alive as I am.\r\nMakes about as much sense as me finding this hand-made camera and typewriter just lying around on the beach. But maybe these picture postcards will prove I ain’t making any of this up. They do say seeing’s believing, right?\r\nAnyway, I'm still trying to work it all out myself. But I promise you, I'm gonna find a way home. Picnic or not, we'll make some fireworks together when I do.\r\nI'll write you again soon Janie, but just now I think I hear a dinner-saur clucking in the bushes.\r\n\r\nI’m so hungry -- BOB\r\n \nP.S. Tell Bill he still owes me that $20 from the big New Year’s poker game, and we ain’t waiting until 1945 to collect.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"亲爱的简,\r\n\r\n独立日那天的野餐会上你大概是见不着我了。我后悔之前没抽时间写信给你, 因为我现在身处一个鬼知道在哪儿的热带海岛上, 真怀疑这里能不能寄信回家。\r\n\r\n我没有瞒着你的意思, 我猜你现在肯定已经听说了, 我根本没有在诺曼底登陆。嗯..是的, 这里连纳粹的鬼影都没有。但是这里的每个人和事都他娘的想弄死我。\r\n\r\n听我说: 这岛上竟然还有喘着气的, 活生生的恐龙。我猜你现在肯定在想: 鲍勃这家伙一定是疯了。但是我说的这些都是实话, 我向你拍胸脯保证, 甚至对着我的老娘在天之灵发誓, 那些玩意儿真的就在这里走来走去的。\r\n\r\n这事儿就跟我在海滩上找到的手工相机跟打字机一样荒唐。但也许这信里的照片可以证明我没有说谎。毕竟人们常说眼见为实, 对吧?\r\n\r\n总而言之, 我还在努力搞清楚这一切。但我向你保证, 我会回来的。不管还赶不赶得上独立日的野餐会, 等我回去了, 我们要一起放个烟花庆祝一下。\r\n\r\n简, 很快我就会再给你写信的, 但现在我得走了, 我听见灌木丛里我可爱的小晚餐在咕咕叫了。\r\n\r\n我好饿啊 -- 鲍勃\r\n\r\nP.S. 告诉比尔, 新年扑克牌大赛那次他还欠我20块钱呢, 我们可不想等到1945年再去要。","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1688778425"}
      //Dear Jane 1笔记翻译
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::1688778425",
      "Source": "Dear Jane,\r\nYou’re probably not gonna be seeing me around the Fourth of July picnic after all. Sure wish I’d gotten around to writing before now, cause I doubt there’s mail service home from wherever it is I’ve found myself. Some tropical island in god-knows-where.\r\nThat’s not me trying to keep secrets. I figure you must’ve heard by now that I never made it ashore in Normandy anyway. Nope, no Ratzis here. But just about everyone and everything else is trying its damnedest to kill me.\r\nGet this: there are living, breathing DINOSAURS on this island. I can guess what you must be thinking right about now: Bobby’s gone clear off his rocker. But I’m writing you hand-on-heart, swear-on-my-dear-Momma’s-grave -- somehow those things are still walking around here, just as alive as I am.\r\nMakes about as much sense as me finding this hand-made camera and typewriter just lying around on the beach. But maybe these picture postcards will prove I ain’t making any of this up. They do say seeing’s believing, right?\r\nAnyway, I'm still trying to work it all out myself. But I promise you, I'm gonna find a way home. Picnic or not, we'll make some fireworks together when I do.\r\nI'll write you again soon Janie, but just now I think I hear a dinner-saur clucking in the bushes.\r\n\r\nI’m so hungry -- BOB\r\n\t\nP.S. Tell Bill he still owes me that $20 from the big New Year’s poker game, and we ain’t waiting until 1945 to collect.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"亲爱的简,\r\n\r\n独立日那天的野餐会上你大概是见不着我了。我后悔之前没抽时间写信给你, 因为我现在身处一个鬼知道在哪儿的热带海岛上, 真怀疑这里能不能寄信回家。\r\n\r\n我没有瞒着你的意思, 我猜你现在肯定已经听说了, 我根本没有在诺曼底登陆。嗯..是的, 这里连纳粹的鬼影都没有。但是这里的每个人和事都他娘的想弄死我。\r\n\r\n听我说: 这岛上竟然还有喘着气的, 活生生的恐龙。我猜你现在肯定在想: 鲍勃这家伙一定是疯了。但是我说的这些都是实话, 我向你拍胸脯保证, 甚至对着我的老娘在天之灵发誓, 那些玩意儿真的就在这里走来走去的。\r\n\r\n这事儿就跟我在海滩上找到的手工相机跟打字机一样荒唐。但也许这信里的照片可以证明我没有说谎。毕竟人们常说眼见为实, 对吧?\r\n\r\n总而言之, 我还在努力搞清楚这一切。但我向你保证, 我会回来的。不管还赶不赶得上独立日的野餐会, 等我回去了, 我们要一起放个烟花庆祝一下。\r\n\r\n简, 很快我就会再给你写信的, 但现在我得走了, 我听见灌木丛里我可爱的小晚餐在咕咕叫了。\r\n\r\n我好饿啊 -- 鲍勃\r\n\r\nP.S. 告诉比尔, 新年扑克牌大赛那次他还欠我20块钱呢, 我们可不想等到1945年再去要。","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
      //Dear Jane 1笔记翻译
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "AE6938084FC04B14520CF19C2847A70B",
      "Source": "Now Jane, before you get all wound up about me spending time with some castaway girl, let me just say you got nothing to worry about on that score. It’s more like when your folks used to make us take your know-it-all kid sister along with us everywhere. You know -- a real pain in the ass.\r\nShe just washed up on my beach, and boy does it show! Doubt the girl would last half a day on this island if I wasn’t here to babysit her. She's too damn soft! The very first time I saw her, she kept me from catching some squab for dinner.\r\nAnd suddenly I’ve got some brat lecturing me about how her precious new pet’s the last of its kind. Wants me to take her seriously, like she’s some kind of expert. All she has to do is look around... I mean, those fat little birds are all over the place here!\r\nI haven’t even told you the nuttiest part, how she claims to be from the FUTURE? At least she says the good guys won, which means you stayed safe and sound stateside.\r\nEither way, I thought I better show the girl what we’re dealing with here: man-eating monsters, floating sky things, the whole nine yards. But maybe I shouldn’t have rushed her. She’s been just staring at all of it, long enough for me to take her picture and write you this note.\r\nDon’t worry, I promise I won’t let her slow me down too much. Nothing’s keeping me from getting back to your home cooking.\r\n\r\nSave me some, baby -- BOB",
      "Trans": {"SC":"简, 在你纠结我和某个跟我同样遭遇的女孩在一起之前, 我想澄清一下, 这个你完全没担心的必要。这种情况下她更像是你爸妈总是让我们去哪儿都带上你那个人小鬼大的妹妹一样。你懂的 -- 真是让人头大。\r\n\r\n这小姑娘很突然地被冲到我这片海滩上, 就那么突兀地出现! 她看上去实在是太娇弱了! 而且一眼就能看出她很不适应这里的生活! 如果没有我在这里照看她, 我真怀疑她能否在这个岛上撑过半天。我第一次见到她的时候, 她甚至还阻止我抓那些雏鸟当晚餐。\r\n\r\n接着, 这小姑娘竟对我喋喋不休, 说她那所谓的珍贵宠物可能是最后一只了, 她想让我摆正对她的态度, 这样子就好像她是什么专家一样。但她只要环顾一下四周就能明白...我想说的是, 那些肥嘟嘟的雏鸟这里到处都是!\r\n\r\n我甚至还没告诉你最离谱的事呢, 她居然声称她来自“未来”! 不过至少她说正义的一方打赢了, 这也意味着你在国内能安然无恙。\r\n\r\n不管怎样, 我觉得我最好是让她看清楚我们的处境: 到处都充斥着吃人的怪兽还有飘在空中的那玩意儿。但或许我不该这么催促她。她只是全神贯注于这周遭的一切, 这时间足够我给她拍个照并写这封信给你。\r\n\r\n不用担心, 我保证她不会太拖我后腿的。没什么能阻止我回到你身边享用你做的大餐。\r\n\r\n亲爱的, 记得给我留点哦 -- 鲍勃","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3200617647"}
      //Dear Jane 2笔记翻译
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::3200617647",
      "Source": "Now Jane, before you get all wound up about me spending time with some castaway girl, let me just say you got nothing to worry about on that score. It’s more like when your folks used to make us take your know-it-all kid sister along with us everywhere. You know -- a real pain in the ass.\r\nShe just washed up on my beach, and boy does it show! Doubt the girl would last half a day on this island if I wasn’t here to babysit her. She's too damn soft! The very first time I saw her, she kept me from catching some squab for dinner.\r\nAnd suddenly I’ve got some brat lecturing me about how her precious new pet’s the last of its kind. Wants me to take her seriously, like she’s some kind of expert. All she has to do is look around... I mean, those fat little birds are all over the place here!\r\nI haven’t even told you the nuttiest part, how she claims to be from the FUTURE? At least she says the good guys won, which means you stayed safe and sound stateside.\r\nEither way, I thought I better show the girl what we’re dealing with here: man-eating monsters, floating sky things, the whole nine yards. But maybe I shouldn’t have rushed her. She’s been just staring at all of it, long enough for me to take her picture and write you this note.\r\nDon’t worry, I promise I won’t let her slow me down too much. Nothing’s keeping me from getting back to your home cooking.\r\n\r\nSave me some, baby -- BOB",
      "Trans": {"SC":"简, 在你纠结我和某个跟我同样遭遇的女孩在一起之前, 我想澄清一下, 这个你完全没担心的必要。这种情况下她更像是你爸妈总是让我们去哪儿都带上你那个人小鬼大的妹妹一样。你懂的 -- 真是让人头大。\r\n\r\n这小姑娘很突然地被冲到我这片海滩上, 就那么突兀地出现! 她看上去实在是太娇弱了! 而且一眼就能看出她很不适应这里的生活! 如果没有我在这里照看她, 我真怀疑她能否在这个岛上撑过半天。我第一次见到她的时候, 她甚至还阻止我抓那些雏鸟当晚餐。\r\n\r\n接着, 这小姑娘竟对我喋喋不休, 说她那所谓的珍贵宠物可能是最后一只了, 她想让我摆正对她的态度, 这样子就好像她是什么专家一样。但她只要环顾一下四周就能明白...我想说的是, 那些肥嘟嘟的雏鸟这里到处都是!\r\n\r\n我甚至还没告诉你最离谱的事呢, 她居然声称她来自“未来”! 不过至少她说正义的一方打赢了, 这也意味着你在国内能安然无恙。\r\n\r\n不管怎样, 我觉得我最好是让她看清楚我们的处境: 到处都充斥着吃人的怪兽还有飘在空中的那玩意儿。但或许我不该这么催促她。她只是全神贯注于这周遭的一切, 这时间足够我给她拍个照并写这封信给你。\r\n\r\n不用担心, 我保证她不会太拖我后腿的。没什么能阻止我回到你身边享用你做的大餐。\r\n\r\n亲爱的, 记得给我留点哦 -- 鲍勃","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
      //Dear Jane 2笔记翻译
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "E559468A4C41C74943084797FEA8A658",
      "Source": "Hey, Janie. Not sure why I’m just getting around to writing home now -- ain’t like I can mail you anything from underground. Maybe you heard -- I never made it to France. Though I guess you wouldn’t know that’s where I was supposed to be headed, before I woke up inside this monster spider nest.\r\nI tell you my skin was crawling, even before I found this home-made camera and typewriter hanging around in a cobweb. Don’t want to think about what happened to the owner, but at least it saves you having to make out my chicken-scratch handwriting.\r\nSeemed like I wandered around in the dark forever, before I managed to throw together a torch and shed some light on my situation. Right away, I wished I hadn’t -- just about everything creeping around down here is too damn big.\r\nIf bugs as long as my arm ain’t weird enough for you, I saw an honest-to-God sabertooth tiger prowling around! I don’t need to tell you I kept my distance from that mean old cat. Not sure how it didn’t smell me -- I must reek to high heaven by now.\r\nGot to sign off now. Something just blew out the cave wall so daylight's shining through! Looks like there’s a tropical jungle out there. I can even hear birds calling. Can’t wait to roast up a few of those, though I’m not looking forward to having to squeeze past an eight-legged carcass the size of a bus.\r\n\r\nBe glad you’re not here too -- BOB",
      "Trans": {"SC":"嘿, 简妮。不晓得为什么拖到现在才往家里写信 -- 毕竟也不是我想就能从地下给你寄东西的。或许你听说了 -- 我没去成法国。尽管我猜你应该不知道, 但至少在这个巨大蜘蛛巢穴里醒来之前, 我本应该是去那里的。\r\n\r\n我跟你说, 在我发现那个自制相机和打字机悬挂在蜘蛛网中之前, 我的鸡皮疙瘩就已经起来了, 我都不敢想象这些东西的主人遭遇了什么, 但至少这样你就不需要费力去辨认我那潦草的字迹了。\r\n\r\n感觉我在黑暗中漫无目的地徘徊了一万年, 直到我终于拼凑出一支火把, 给我目前的处境带来了一丝光明。可下一秒, 我就后悔了 -- 因为在这里爬动着的几乎所有东西都大得吓人。\r\n\r\n如果说像我手臂一样长的虫子你都觉得不足为奇的话, 那么我还看到了一只货真价实的刃齿虎在周边徘徊! 不用说, 我肯定跟那只凶悍的大猫保持足够多的距离。不确定它为什么没嗅到我。-- 想必我已经臭气熏天了。\r\n\r\n就先到这吧, 刚才有东西炸穿了洞穴的岩壁, 阳光正从洞口透进来! 看起来外面是一片热带丛林。我甚至能听到鸟儿的叫声。真想去烤几只来尝尝。虽然不太情愿, 但我还是不得不从这个长着八条腿且有公交车大小的尸骸边挤过。\r\n\r\n我很庆幸你没跟我一样在这里 -- 鲍勃","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3458487862"}
      //Dear Jane 3笔记翻译
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::3458487862",
      "Source": "Hey, Janie. Not sure why I’m just getting around to writing home now -- ain’t like I can mail you anything from underground. Maybe you heard -- I never made it to France. Though I guess you wouldn’t know that’s where I was supposed to be headed, before I woke up inside this monster spider nest.\r\nI tell you my skin was crawling, even before I found this home-made camera and typewriter hanging around in a cobweb. Don’t want to think about what happened to the owner, but at least it saves you having to make out my chicken-scratch handwriting.\r\nSeemed like I wandered around in the dark forever, before I managed to throw together a torch and shed some light on my situation. Right away, I wished I hadn’t -- just about everything creeping around down here is too damn big.\r\nIf bugs as long as my arm ain’t weird enough for you, I saw an honest-to-God sabertooth tiger prowling around! I don’t need to tell you I kept my distance from that mean old cat. Not sure how it didn’t smell me -- I must reek to high heaven by now.\r\nGot to sign off now. Something just blew out the cave wall so daylight's shining through! Looks like there’s a tropical jungle out there. I can even hear birds calling. Can’t wait to roast up a few of those, though I’m not looking forward to having to squeeze past an eight-legged carcass the size of a bus.\r\n\r\nBe glad you’re not here too -- BOB",
      "Trans": {"SC":"嘿, 简妮。不晓得为什么拖到现在才往家里写信 -- 毕竟也不是我想就能从地下给你寄东西的。或许你听说了 -- 我没去成法国。尽管我猜你应该不知道, 但至少在这个巨大蜘蛛巢穴里醒来之前, 我本应该是去那里的。\r\n\r\n我跟你说, 在我发现那个自制相机和打字机悬挂在蜘蛛网中之前, 我的鸡皮疙瘩就已经起来了, 我都不敢想象这些东西的主人遭遇了什么, 但至少这样你就不需要费力去辨认我那潦草的字迹了。\r\n\r\n感觉我在黑暗中漫无目的地徘徊了一万年, 直到我终于拼凑出一支火把, 给我目前的处境带来了一丝光明。可下一秒, 我就后悔了 -- 因为在这里爬动着的几乎所有东西都大得吓人。\r\n\r\n如果说像我手臂一样长的虫子你都觉得不足为奇的话, 那么我还看到了一只货真价实的刃齿虎在周边徘徊! 不用说, 我肯定跟那只凶悍的大猫保持足够多的距离。不确定它为什么没嗅到我。-- 想必我已经臭气熏天了。\r\n\r\n就先到这吧, 刚才有东西炸穿了洞穴的岩壁, 阳光正从洞口透进来! 看起来外面是一片热带丛林。我甚至能听到鸟儿的叫声。真想去烤几只来尝尝。虽然不太情愿, 但我还是不得不从这个长着八条腿且有公交车大小的尸骸边挤过。\r\n\r\n我很庆幸你没跟我一样在这里 -- 鲍勃","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
      //Dear Jane 3笔记翻译
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "F12CA6B04EE3E39017D7969A9FB37734",
      "Source": "Janie, you wouldn’t believe what I’ve been through since I crawled out of that nice, safe cave. Feel pretty dumb for giving up a perfectly good hidey-hole over a few bugs. I traded cool peace and quiet for a steaming forest full of freaks.\r\nI’m talking actual, real life dinosaurs, stomping and flapping around as if they didn’t all die out a zillion years ago. Did the Nazis fire some kind of time ray at us? Cause if I’m lost in the past, I got no idea how to find my way home to you.\r\nClimbing up that mountain didn’t help me figure anything out either. Dinos from here to the sea, with no sign of civilization other than some shiny floaty towers that don’t look all that prehistorical. I don’t wanna think about those things too hard.\r\nLeast I had this camera along so I could show you what I’ve been running from. Sure I’m hungry, but I wasn’t about to go anywhere near those giant nests, eggs or no. Still, something riled up those big bat-birds enough to chase me back down the mountain and into the woods.\r\nBarely survived getting dive-bombed long enough to get bushwhacked by some goons in armor, riding on rats big as horses. They say they’re taking me to some kind of prison camp upriver. Can’t say I like the sound of that.\r\n\r\nIf it ain’t one thing, it’s another -- BOB",
      "Trans": {"SC":"简妮, 你一定会对我爬出这舒适且安全的洞穴之后又经历了些什么感到难以置信。就因为几只虫子而放弃一个完美的藏身之处, 我简直蠢爆了。我拿荫凉和安宁换来了个满是怪物的闷热丛林。\r\n\r\n我是指实实在在的, 活生生的恐龙, 它们踩踏着, 扑腾着, 就好像几亿年前它们根本就没有灭绝一样。难道纳粹朝我们发射了某种时光射线? 如果我真的被困在了过去, 我就不知道该怎么回去, 回到你身边了。\r\n\r\n爬上那座山也没有帮我厘清任何头绪。从这里到海边全是恐龙, 除了一些看起来不太像是史前时期的闪光漂浮塔外, 没有一点文明的迹象。我真不想太深入地思考这些事情。\r\n\r\n还好我带了这台相机, 所以我才能向你展示我在逃离什么。我着实饿了, 但我也绝不靠近那些巨大的巢穴, 不管有没有蛋在里面。尽管如此, 还是有什么东西激怒了那些蝙蝠一样的鸟, 以至于它们追着我下山跑进了树林里。\r\n\r\n我勉强躲过它们的俯冲式攻击, 但是没过多久就被一些武装暴徒袭击了, 他们骑着马一样大的老鼠。他们说要把我带去河流上游的集中营里去。这听起来实在不太妙。\r\n\r\n真是一波未平, 一波又起 -- 鲍勃","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2044729805"}
      //Dear Jane 4笔记翻译
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::2044729805",
      "Source": "Janie, you wouldn’t believe what I’ve been through since I crawled out of that nice, safe cave. Feel pretty dumb for giving up a perfectly good hidey-hole over a few bugs. I traded cool peace and quiet for a steaming forest full of freaks.\r\nI’m talking actual, real life dinosaurs, stomping and flapping around as if they didn’t all die out a zillion years ago. Did the Nazis fire some kind of time ray at us? Cause if I’m lost in the past, I got no idea how to find my way home to you.\r\nClimbing up that mountain didn’t help me figure anything out either. Dinos from here to the sea, with no sign of civilization other than some shiny floaty towers that don’t look all that prehistorical. I don’t wanna think about those things too hard.\r\nLeast I had this camera along so I could show you what I’ve been running from. Sure I’m hungry, but I wasn’t about to go anywhere near those giant nests, eggs or no. Still, something riled up those big bat-birds enough to chase me back down the mountain and into the woods.\r\nBarely survived getting dive-bombed long enough to get bushwhacked by some goons in armor, riding on rats big as horses. They say they’re taking me to some kind of prison camp upriver. Can’t say I like the sound of that.\r\n\r\nIf it ain’t one thing, it’s another -- BOB",
      "Trans": {"SC":"简妮, 你一定会对我爬出这舒适且安全的洞穴之后又经历了些什么感到难以置信。就因为几只虫子而放弃一个完美的藏身之处, 我简直蠢爆了。我拿荫凉和安宁换来了个满是怪物的闷热丛林。\r\n\r\n我是指实实在在的, 活生生的恐龙, 它们踩踏着, 扑腾着, 就好像几亿年前它们根本就没有灭绝一样。难道纳粹朝我们发射了某种时光射线? 如果我真的被困在了过去, 我就不知道该怎么回去, 回到你身边了。\r\n\r\n爬上那座山也没有帮我厘清任何头绪。从这里到海边全是恐龙, 除了一些看起来不太像是史前时期的闪光漂浮塔外, 没有一点文明的迹象。我真不想太深入地思考这些事情。\r\n\r\n还好我带了这台相机, 所以我才能向你展示我在逃离什么。我着实饿了, 但我也绝不靠近那些巨大的巢穴, 不管有没有蛋在里面。尽管如此, 还是有什么东西激怒了那些蝙蝠一样的鸟, 以至于它们追着我下山跑进了树林里。\r\n\r\n我勉强躲过它们的俯冲式攻击, 但是没过多久就被一些武装暴徒袭击了, 他们骑着马一样大的老鼠。他们说要把我带去河流上游的集中营里去。这听起来实在不太妙。\r\n\r\n真是一波未平, 一波又起 -- 鲍勃","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
      //Dear Jane 4笔记翻译
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "95AA36C14F11BF5F3F7F609E1664EA45",
      "Source": "Janie, I’m free! Didn’t think I’d ever be able to write you again, after those rat-riders put me to work in their mine. They confiscated my gear at the gate and tried to get me to wear a secondhand prison outfit. Those rags stunk like someone had just died in em, so I said thanks but no thanks. I’d rather work in my altogether.\r\nI was sorry real quick I turned down any way to cover up, after I got put to work under that hot sun. By the end of the first day I had blisters on my blisters. And after sundown it was like out of the frying pan and into the freezer.\r\nAll the damn mist coming off the river clung to everything. And they locked us up deep in the dark and cold. And it wasn’t like we got blankets or turndown service there. No lullabies or pillows with mints on em.\r\nBelieve it or not, this little girl was the one who started our jailbreak. She caught an armload of monster centipedes that we had crawling all over to help her break us out. Turns out their spit can melt right through iron chains!\r\nWas planning to do more to help before I got knocked on my ass in a stampede of those big cart-pulling armadillo things. By the time I finally came to again, it was all over and the place was deserted. Can’t blame everyone for wanting to get out while the getting’s good.\r\n\r\nBack into the woods, I guess -- BOB",
      "Trans": {"SC":"简妮, 我自由了! 在被那些骑老鼠的家伙扔到矿坑给他们干活之后, 真没想到还能再次给你写信。他们在大门前没收了我的装备, 并且试图让我穿上二手的囚服。\r\n那些破布闻起来就像有人刚死在里面一样, 所以我谢绝了。我宁可光着身子干活。\r\n\r\n开始在如此炽热的阳光下劳作后, 我很快就对之前立马拒绝了任何遮蔽物而感到后悔了。第一天快结束的时候, 我被晒得体无完肤。日落之后, 这滋味, 简直可以用水深火热来形容。\r\n\r\n那该死的雾气从河边升起, 笼罩了这里的一切。他们把我们锁在又黑又冷的深处。这里也不像是能得到毛毯或床铺的地方。没有摇篮曲, 更没有放了薄荷糖的枕头。\r\n\r\n不管你信不信, 这个小女孩是我们越狱的开路先锋。她抓了一把在周围爬行的怪物蜈蚣来帮助我们逃脱。原来它们的唾液可以直接融化铁链!\r\n\r\n在我被那拖车一样大的犰狳撞倒在地之前, 我本计划做更多的事情来帮助大家, 但是当我再次醒来时, 一切都结束了, 那地方已经空无一人。人人都想着趁乱逃离, 这也怪不得别人。\r\n\r\n我猜, 又得回到丛林了 -- 鲍勃","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1142152334"}
      //Dear Jane 5笔记翻译
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::1142152334",
      "Source": "Janie, I’m free! Didn’t think I’d ever be able to write you again, after those rat-riders put me to work in their mine. They confiscated my gear at the gate and tried to get me to wear a secondhand prison outfit. Those rags stunk like someone had just died in em, so I said thanks but no thanks. I’d rather work in my altogether.\r\nI was sorry real quick I turned down any way to cover up, after I got put to work under that hot sun. By the end of the first day I had blisters on my blisters. And after sundown it was like out of the frying pan and into the freezer.\r\nAll the damn mist coming off the river clung to everything. And they locked us up deep in the dark and cold. And it wasn’t like we got blankets or turndown service there. No lullabies or pillows with mints on em.\r\nBelieve it or not, this little girl was the one who started our jailbreak. She caught an armload of monster centipedes that we had crawling all over to help her break us out. Turns out their spit can melt right through iron chains!\r\nWas planning to do more to help before I got knocked on my ass in a stampede of those big cart-pulling armadillo things. By the time I finally came to again, it was all over and the place was deserted. Can’t blame everyone for wanting to get out while the getting’s good.\r\n\r\nBack into the woods, I guess -- BOB",
      "Trans": {"SC":"简妮, 我自由了! 在被那些骑老鼠的家伙扔到矿坑给他们干活之后, 真没想到还能再次给你写信。他们在大门前没收了我的装备, 并且试图让我穿上二手的囚服。\r\n那些破布闻起来就像有人刚死在里面一样, 所以我谢绝了。我宁可光着身子干活。\r\n\r\n开始在如此炽热的阳光下劳作后, 我很快就对之前立马拒绝了任何遮蔽物而感到后悔了。第一天快结束的时候, 我被晒得体无完肤。日落之后, 这滋味, 简直可以用水深火热来形容。\r\n\r\n那该死的雾气从河边升起, 笼罩了这里的一切。他们把我们锁在又黑又冷的深处。这里也不像是能得到毛毯或床铺的地方。没有摇篮曲, 更没有放了薄荷糖的枕头。\r\n\r\n不管你信不信, 这个小女孩是我们越狱的开路先锋。她抓了一把在周围爬行的怪物蜈蚣来帮助我们逃脱。原来它们的唾液可以直接融化铁链!\r\n\r\n在我被那拖车一样大的犰狳撞倒在地之前, 我本计划做更多的事情来帮助大家, 但是当我再次醒来时, 一切都结束了, 那地方已经空无一人。人人都想着趁乱逃离, 这也怪不得别人。\r\n\r\n我猜, 又得回到丛林了 -- 鲍勃","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
      //Dear Jane 5笔记翻译
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "225EA6EE43A502C73B8FC4B0DA708215",
      "Source": "I swear I can’t seem to catch a break, Janie.\r\nAlmost threw in with some folks building Swiss Family Robinson-style houses up in the trees. Getting above it all sure seemed like a great idea to me. But then I couldn’t help noticing this outfit was gearing up for a fight.\r\nIt was like boot camp all over again, except I don’t remember any Chinese lady sergeants there drilling recruits with pig-stickers. Besides, I wasn’t keen about enlisting in a brand-new war so soon after I’d gone AWOL from another.\r\nSo I struck out on my own, but not too far. Thought there might be something to that safety in numbers idea, in case those guys from the mine came back to make an example of us escapees. I spent a few days building a nice tree fort all my own, off to one side of Toothpick Terraces.\r\nNo sooner did I have my place all set up just the way I liked, when the bad guys showed up. I knew we were in for it when I saw they had artillery mounted on dinosaurs. And sure enough, they started raining hell on us! All that work for nothing...\r\nIn the middle of the mess I managed to spot the kid from the mine again, the one who broke us out. You’d think I would have learned by now to stick with her, but no. I heard her yelling to run into the swamps, and decided I might do better going the opposite way.\r\n\r\nAlready thinking I might’ve screwed up again -- BOB",
      "Trans": {"SC":"命运真是爱跟我开玩笑啊, 简妮。\r\n\r\n我差点就加入一个原生态的树屋部落了, 我看他们氛围融洽, 团结一心。对我而言, 跟着他们归隐山林倒像是个不错的主意。但是后来, 我留意到他们的服饰好像是随时为战争而做准备的。\r\n\r\n这感觉就好像是再次回到训练营一样, 只不过我当时没见过中国女军士用野猪矛在操练新兵。此外, 我刚从一场战争中脱身, 就更没兴趣卷入另一场了。\r\n\r\n所以我选择了单独行动, 其实也没走太远。因为我想到跟着大部队待在一起还是会更安全一些, 毕竟矿坑那伙人可不会轻易地就放过我们这些逃犯。于是我花了几天时间, 在那层层叠叠的树屋平台一侧建造了一个独属于我的树屋, 它可太棒了。\r\n\r\n就在我按自己的喜好把这地方布置完的时候, 那些恶棍就出现了。当我看到他们在恐龙背上安装了火炮的时候, 我就知道我们要有大麻烦了。果不其然, 炮弹如雨点般向我们袭来! 我之前所做的一切都付之东流了...\r\n\r\n混乱中我再次发现了在矿坑中解救我们的那个孩子。你可能以为我会跟着她, 但并没有。我听见她大声呼喊 -- 往沼泽里跑。这次我觉得反其道而行之可能会更好。\r\n\r\n我想我可能又要搞砸了 -- 鲍勃","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2341089138"}
      //Dear Jane 6笔记翻译
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::2341089138",
      "Source": "I swear I can’t seem to catch a break, Janie.\r\nAlmost threw in with some folks building Swiss Family Robinson-style houses up in the trees. Getting above it all sure seemed like a great idea to me. But then I couldn’t help noticing this outfit was gearing up for a fight.\r\nIt was like boot camp all over again, except I don’t remember any Chinese lady sergeants there drilling recruits with pig-stickers. Besides, I wasn’t keen about enlisting in a brand-new war so soon after I’d gone AWOL from another.\r\nSo I struck out on my own, but not too far. Thought there might be something to that safety in numbers idea, in case those guys from the mine came back to make an example of us escapees. I spent a few days building a nice tree fort all my own, off to one side of Toothpick Terraces.\r\nNo sooner did I have my place all set up just the way I liked, when the bad guys showed up. I knew we were in for it when I saw they had artillery mounted on dinosaurs. And sure enough, they started raining hell on us! All that work for nothing...\r\nIn the middle of the mess I managed to spot the kid from the mine again, the one who broke us out. You’d think I would have learned by now to stick with her, but no. I heard her yelling to run into the swamps, and decided I might do better going the opposite way.\r\n\r\nAlready thinking I might’ve screwed up again -- BOB",
      "Trans": {"SC":"命运真是爱跟我开玩笑啊, 简妮。\r\n\r\n我差点就加入一个原生态的树屋部落了, 我看他们氛围融洽, 团结一心。对我而言, 跟着他们归隐山林倒像是个不错的主意。但是后来, 我留意到他们的服饰好像是随时为战争而做准备的。\r\n\r\n这感觉就好像是再次回到训练营一样, 只不过我当时没见过中国女军士用野猪矛在操练新兵。此外, 我刚从一场战争中脱身, 就更没兴趣卷入另一场了。\r\n\r\n所以我选择了单独行动, 其实也没走太远。因为我想到跟着大部队待在一起还是会更安全一些, 毕竟矿坑那伙人可不会轻易地就放过我们这些逃犯。于是我花了几天时间, 在那层层叠叠的树屋平台一侧建造了一个独属于我的树屋, 它可太棒了。\r\n\r\n就在我按自己的喜好把这地方布置完的时候, 那些恶棍就出现了。当我看到他们在恐龙背上安装了火炮的时候, 我就知道我们要有大麻烦了。果不其然, 炮弹如雨点般向我们袭来! 我之前所做的一切都付之东流了...\r\n\r\n混乱中我再次发现了在矿坑中解救我们的那个孩子。你可能以为我会跟着她, 但并没有。我听见她大声呼喊 -- 往沼泽里跑。这次我觉得反其道而行之可能会更好。\r\n\r\n我想我可能又要搞砸了 -- 鲍勃","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
      //Dear Jane 6笔记翻译
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "5799E52C48C8E4AC7BE7C4A95BD16912",
      "Source": "Dear Janie, I definitely made a big mistake running away from everyone else from Treehouse Company. And that’s not just cause I ended up running straight back to where the bad guys came from. I’m also realizing how much harder it is to get by out here on my own.\r\nI’ve been stuck behind enemy lines, trying to survive off whatever scraps I can scrounge outside that stone fortress of theirs. After a day or so of watching some of the local thieving rat-lizards sneak in and out of the fort like it was nothing, I thought I’d rob them instead. Better to let the critters take all the risk, I figured.\r\nI was all set to spear one when a bomb went off inside the fortress! The blast wave knocked me right off my feet, and that whiskery little bastard ran off with his haul of carrots before I even could think of going after him.\r\nDidn’t have much time for bellyaching before I heard a roar like none other, that sent a shiver right down my spine.b Couldn’t tell what the hell was going down in there, but I know a fight to the death when I hear one.\r\nI was all set to play soldier one last time and charge into battle, but something exploded inside the fort and collapsed my only way in. I just hope that any good guys in that scrap were OK.\r\nFor now, I think I’m gonna take a long breather, and stop getting involved in one snafu after another. ‘Sides, I think I see that thieving rat-lizard again, and it looks like it’s carrying an... axe?\r\nSomething mighty familiar about that axe...\r\n\r\nYours forever -- BOB",
      "Trans": {"SC":"亲爱的简妮, 远离树屋部落的人逃难真的是大错特错。我不但直愣愣地跑向了那伙恶棍前进的方向, 而且我后知后觉地发现独自一人想要活着离开这儿有多难。\r\n\r\n我被困在敌人战线的后方, 试图在他们的要塞外围翻找一些残汤剩饭来充饥。经过一天左右的观察, 我发现一些当地爱偷东西的鼠蜥如入无人之境般在要塞中进进出出, 我想着, 去抢它们带出来的东西好像也不错, 最好是让那些小家伙替我承担所有风险。\r\n\r\n就当我准备用长矛刺向其中一只时, 要塞里边突然发生了爆炸! 冲击波直接把我震倒在地, 我还没来得及想到要追上去, 那长满须子的小混蛋就带着它偷来的胡萝卜逃之夭夭了。\r\n\r\n还没来得及抱怨, 我就先听到一声前所未闻的咆哮, 那声音让我脊背发凉。我不清楚里面发生了什么事, 但那声咆哮让我明白, 这肯定是一场恶战。\r\n\r\n我本想最后一次作为一个士兵冲入战场, 但是要塞里的某些东西发生了爆炸, 堵住了我唯一可以进去的路。我现在只能盼着这场混战中的好人都没什么大碍。\r\n\r\n现在, 我要打算好好休息一下, 不想再卷入一个又一个的麻烦。呃..我想我又看到了那个偷东西的鼠蜥了, 它看起来好像带了一把...斧头?\r\n\r\n那把斧头看起来有点眼熟...\r\n\r\n永远爱你 -- 鲍勃","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"892247345"}
      //Dear Jane 7笔记翻译
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::892247345",
      "Source": "Dear Janie, I definitely made a big mistake running away from everyone else from Treehouse Company. And that’s not just cause I ended up running straight back to where the bad guys came from. I’m also realizing how much harder it is to get by out here on my own.\r\nI’ve been stuck behind enemy lines, trying to survive off whatever scraps I can scrounge outside that stone fortress of theirs. After a day or so of watching some of the local thieving rat-lizards sneak in and out of the fort like it was nothing, I thought I’d rob them instead. Better to let the critters take all the risk, I figured.\r\nI was all set to spear one when a bomb went off inside the fortress! The blast wave knocked me right off my feet, and that whiskery little bastard ran off with his haul of carrots before I even could think of going after him.\r\nDidn’t have much time for bellyaching before I heard a roar like none other, that sent a shiver right down my spine.b Couldn’t tell what the hell was going down in there, but I know a fight to the death when I hear one.\r\nI was all set to play soldier one last time and charge into battle, but something exploded inside the fort and collapsed my only way in. I just hope that any good guys in that scrap were OK.\r\nFor now, I think I’m gonna take a long breather, and stop getting involved in one snafu after another. ‘Sides, I think I see that thieving rat-lizard again, and it looks like it’s carrying an... axe?\r\nSomething mighty familiar about that axe...\r\n\r\nYours forever -- BOB",
      "Trans": {"SC":"亲爱的简妮, 远离树屋部落的人逃难真的是大错特错。我不但直愣愣地跑向了那伙恶棍前进的方向, 而且我后知后觉地发现独自一人想要活着离开这儿有多难。\r\n\r\n我被困在敌人战线的后方, 试图在他们的要塞外围翻找一些残汤剩饭来充饥。经过一天左右的观察, 我发现一些当地爱偷东西的鼠蜥如入无人之境般在要塞中进进出出, 我想着, 去抢它们带出来的东西好像也不错, 最好是让那些小家伙替我承担所有风险。\r\n\r\n就当我准备用长矛刺向其中一只时, 要塞里边突然发生了爆炸! 冲击波直接把我震倒在地, 我还没来得及想到要追上去, 那长满须子的小混蛋就带着它偷来的胡萝卜逃之夭夭了。\r\n\r\n还没来得及抱怨, 我就先听到一声前所未闻的咆哮, 那声音让我脊背发凉。我不清楚里面发生了什么事, 但那声咆哮让我明白, 这肯定是一场恶战。\r\n\r\n我本想最后一次作为一个士兵冲入战场, 但是要塞里的某些东西发生了爆炸, 堵住了我唯一可以进去的路。我现在只能盼着这场混战中的好人都没什么大碍。\r\n\r\n现在, 我要打算好好休息一下, 不想再卷入一个又一个的麻烦。呃..我想我又看到了那个偷东西的鼠蜥了, 它看起来好像带了一把...斧头?\r\n\r\n那把斧头看起来有点眼熟...\r\n\r\n永远爱你 -- 鲍勃","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
      //Dear Jane 7笔记翻译
    },
    {
