    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::2823858614",
      "Source": "Fasolasuchus Dossier",
      "Trans": {"SC":"法索拉鳄图鉴","JA":"法索拉鳄圖鑒"},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::347712335",
      "Source": "Rider Imprinted %i%%\nDamage +%i%%\nResistance +%i%%",
      "Trans": {"SC":"骑手留痕 %i%%\n伤害 +%i%%\n抗性 +%i%%","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::3733177779",
      "Source": "Species: Fasolasuchus sabulonatator \n Time: Late Triassic \n Diet: Carnivore \n Temperament: Aggressive (Ambusher) \n \n Wild \n This wasteland’s full of surprises, and not exactly the good kind. There’s something out here that looks like Fasolasuchus, if those proto-crocs could swim through sand like water… \n These beasts might pop up suddenly to ambush you, or swim around you fast enough to catch you in a sand-whirlpool. I can't stress enough how dangerous this deathtrap can be! Plus their tails are strong enough to whip up sand to blind predators and prey alike. \n If you can help it, I recommend staying clear of those spikes. I think they’ve got acid glands at the base of their spiny fins, and in their mouths as well. Their caustic bite seems to melt through the thickest hide. \n \n Domesticated \n One of these monster sand-swimmers would make a great mount, but good luck slowing down something that can shrug off most narcotics. You could try softening one up with explosives, grabbing a spike, and steering it into a rock… But you’d have to be a bit mental to try. \n I imagine the adrenaline junkies able to tame a Fasolasuchus would earn themselves a formidable ride through these scorching sands. They seem to have adapted to fighting larger prey, so I'd advise any faso-rider to steer clear of packs of smaller creatures that can swarm over its defenses.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"通用名称: 法索拉鳄\r\n拉丁学名: Fasolasuchus sabulonatator\r\n正式名称: 沙旋法索拉鳄\r\n时期: 三叠纪晚期\r\n食性: 肉食\r\n性情: 好战 (伏击)\r\n\r\n\r\n野生\r\n这片荒野充斥着\"惊喜\", 实际上可算不得什么好事。这有一种看起来像法索拉鳄的生物, 跟那些远古鳄鱼不同的是, 它能像在水里一样穿梭于沙地中...\r\n这些野兽可能会伏击着, 给与出其不意的袭击, 也可能是在你周围快速地游动, 将你卷入流沙漩涡之中。这死亡漩涡的危险性, 我再怎么强调都不为过! 此外, 它们的尾巴相当强壮, 扬起来的沙子能使捕食者和猎物通通失明。\r\n如果听得进劝, 我建议你远离那些尖刺。我认为它们的刺鳍和口中都有酸液腺。它们带有腐蚀性的撕咬似乎可以腐蚀最坚韧的皮肤。\r\n\r\n\r\n家养\r\n一只这样的沙海泳怪会是非常理想的坐骑, 但要让这样一只能免疫大多数麻醉剂的家伙消停下来, 就只能祝你好运了。你可以试着用爆炸物让它短暂晕厥, 然后抓住刺鳍, 将它引向并撞击岩石...但你得想清楚了再去尝试。\r\n可以想象, 那些常年在刀尖上舔血的人成功驯化一只法索拉鳄并骑着它在沙海驰骋, 是一种怎样壮阔的场景。它们似乎已适应了与大型猎物战斗, 所以我建议每个法索拉鳄骑手都避开那些可以一拥而上倾覆其防御的小型生物群体。","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::1685074115",
      "Source": "Common Name: Oasisaur \nSpecies: Oasisaur zurzura \nTime: Unknown \nDiet: Herbivore \nTemperament: Friendly \n \nWild \nWhere do I start with Oasisaur zurzura? Like most of the unique wildlife I’ve encountered here, this flying island feels like something from legendary fantasy. It’s as big as a Titanosaur, but somehow it can still defy gravity! \nMy hunch is that Oasisaur consumes great bunches of vegetation at once, so a handful of berries wouldn’t be an enticing enough offering. You’d have better luck courting its affection with a topiary or potted shrub, as long as you’re ready to chase rival suitors off the behemoth’s back. \nThis roaming oasis carries soil on its back so fertile that anything planted in it will flourish, even if practically ignored. And that back seems like it has room enough for a small neighborhood...  \n \nDomesticated \nThis living landmass will nurture its longer-term inhabitants. That friendship is worth the time investment, because favored residents get access to a pool with truly miraculous properties. For starters, its restorative waters will cure bathers of nearly any illness or affliction. \nMost unbelievably, the wellspring of an Oasisaur can reincarnate your lost animal friends! Whether by transcendental magic or access to the mysterious technologies of these ARKs, I’ve seen a fallen pet returned to newborn life by committing their essence to that rejuvenating pool. \n",
      "Trans": {"SC":"通用名称: 绿洲龙\r\n拉丁学名: Oasisaur zurzura\r\n正式名称: 幻城绿洲龙\r\n时代: 未知\r\n食性: 植食\r\n性情: 友善\r\n\r\n\r\n野生\r\n我该从何谈起幻城绿洲龙? 它就像我在这里遇到的大多数的奇特动物一样, 这个飞行岛屿就像传说中的幻想生物。尽管它如同泰坦巨龙一般庞大, 但不知为何, 它仍然能够脱离地心引力的控制!\r\n直觉告诉我, 绿洲龙一次就要消耗巨量的植物, 因此对它来说区区一把浆果根本不足为诱。只要准备好驱离这只巨兽背部的侵犯者, 就能通过修剪好的绿雕或盆栽灌木来取悦它。\r\n这座漫游的绿洲上承载着肥沃的土壤, 即使不去打理, 其效果也足以使任何作物茁壮成长。而且, 它的背部空间似乎足以承载一个小型社区...\r\n\r\n\r\n家养\r\n这片生命之土会滋养长期居住在上面的生灵。维系与绿洲龙的友谊是完全值得的, 因为受其垂青的居民, 可以使用一池具有神奇功效的泉水。比如, 这种生命之水能治愈几乎所有的疾病或痛楚。\r\n而最令人难以置信的部分是, 绿洲龙的源泉可以让你死去的动物朋友转世重生! 不管其原理是超自然的魔法, 还是方舟的神秘科技, 我曾亲眼见证了一只逝去的宠物, 在将它的精魄投入生命之泉后, 竟奇迹般地回到了新生的状态。","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::3402294602",
      "Source": "Bob:  Ya know, kid... sooner or later, you’re going to have to talk about it. ",
      "Trans": {"SC":"鲍勃:  你知道的, 孩子...早晚你都得谈谈这事儿。","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
      //鲍勃图鉴-废土-序幕1
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::1323970789",
      "Source": "Bob:  What are you drawing over there anyway?wing over there, anyway?",
      //wing over there, anyway?是多余的
      "Trans": {"SC":"鲍勃:  你在那边画什么呢?","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
      //鲍勃图鉴-废土-序幕1
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::784149088",
