    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::482619303",
      "Source": "Species: Dreadnoughtus recalcitrans\r\nTime: Late Cretaceous\r\nDiet: Herbivore\r\nTemperament: Territorial\r\n\r\nWild\r\nDreadnoughtus was a newly-described fossil genus in my day, named for the idea that it was so large it must’ve had nothing to fear in its own time. The current species does its namesake proud, and may even be able to defy the Titans ruling our post-apocalyptic world.\r\n\r\n\r\nA big believer in picking on creatures its own size, Dreadnoughtus will ignore anything smaller than a Spinosaur to focus on larger threats. It absorbs the fury of incoming attacks to charge up its uncanny, Element-disrupting bellow. Even then, this bruiser shows extraordinary patience, waiting until the last possible moment to come roaring back.\r\n\r\nDomesticated\r\nOnce tamed, Dreadnoughtus will gladly shoulder your heaviest artillery and carry it -- and you -- into battle, on a platform big enough to earn that ‘dreadnought’ name. Your walking war-machine will swallow boulders (or cannonballs!) to spit back up as acid-coated ammo.\r\n\r\n\r\nIf you’re going to war with Titans, it just makes sense to recruit a titanic creature with a grudge against them. Your Dreadnoughtus ally may go down fighting, but not before softening up the adversary for a killing blow. Best of luck, and give ‘em Hell for me!\r\n",
      "Trans": {"SC":"通用名称: 无畏巨龙\r\n拉丁学名: Dreadnoughtus recalcitrans\r\n正式名称: 不屈无畏巨龙\r\n时代: 晚白垩纪\r\n食性: 植食\r\n性情: 强领地意识\r\n\r\n\r\n野生\r\n无畏巨龙是一个在我的时代新描述的化石属, 顾名思义, 巨大的体型一定让它在身处的时代无所畏惧。而如今的物种则将延续这一名称的荣耀, 它甚至绝不屈从于我们后灾变时代泰坦的高压统治。\r\n无与伦比的体型赋予了无畏巨龙极大的自信, 它漠视任何小于棘龙尺寸的生物, 专注迎战更大的威胁。通过承受来势汹汹的怒火攻势, 无畏巨龙能为其难以理解解释的元素干扰咆哮进行充能。即便如此, 这位勇猛的无畏悍将仍然保持了超凡的克制力, 直到最后一刻才会咆哮反击。\r\n\r\n\r\n家养\r\n一旦驯化, 无畏巨龙将义不容辞地肩负起你最沉重的火力, 名副其实地如同“无畏舰”般巨大的战争平台驶向战场。你的行走战争机器将吞下巨石(或炮弹!), 在转化成覆酸弹药之后喷吐出去。\r\n如果你准备向泰坦宣战, 将这样一个和泰坦不共戴天的无畏巨兽纳入麾下, 完全满足你的需要。虽然你的无畏巨龙盟友随时可能在战斗中倒下, 但绝对足以助你削弱对手, 由你予以剩下的致命一击, 并实现最终的胜利。代我将它们送入地狱, 祝君武运昌隆。","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::278771044",
      "Source": "Armadoggo Dossier",
      "Trans": {"SC":"铠护犬图鉴","JA":"铠护犬圖鑒"},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::2645276728",
      "Source": "Armadoggo",
      "Trans": {"SC":"铠护犬","JA":"鎧護犬"},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":true,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::1229005984",
      "Source": "Companion Whistle",
      //这个是干啥的来着, 忘记了.
      "Trans": {"SC":"随伴哨子","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::2976659729",
      "Source": "Common Name: Armadoggo\r\nSpecies: Canis fodiensocius\r\nTime: Late Anthropocene\r\nDiet: Omnivore (but prefers meat)\r\nTemperament: Bestest!\r\n\r\nWild\r\nI’m told this clever canine was commonly sighted in areas contaminated by Element a few centuries after my time, so it may be one of the few lifeforms to have survived the collapse of the ecosphere. Like the dogs of my day, this is a social animal that hunts smaller prey in packs.\r\n\r\nThat bony, scaled shell likely protects Armadoggo from radiation while also allowing it to burrow through the ground. It can cross long distances tunneling under the surface to avoid larger threats. It doesn’t seem threatened by us, and is in fact unusually curious about humans.\r\n\r\nDomesticated\r\nArmadoggo seems happier once tamed and eager to help, much like its pampered cousins from my time. And it’s one fiercely protective pet, alerting you to nearby dangers and even keeping some at bay.\r\n\r\nArmadoggo turns out to have a knack for tracking down valuable technological trinkets hoarded by some of the corrupted local wildlife. Once it picks up the scent from an Element-poisoned kill, it will take you to its hoarded, eminently weaponizable treasure.\r\n\r\nNo leash training needed -- your loyal new companion will happily carry gear and armaments while never straying too far away. If your Armadoggo gets hurt, it’s smart enough to hide away underground where it can lick its wounds until it can rejoin you. Looking around at the mess we made of the world, I’m not sure we deserve their devotion.\r\n",
      "Trans": {"SC":"通用名称: 铠护犬\r\n拉丁学名: Canis fodiensocius\r\n正式名称: 掘地随伴犬\r\n时代: 晚期人类世\r\n食性: 杂食 (更喜欢吃肉)\r\n性情: 超乖的!\r\n\r\n\r\n野生\r\nI’m told this clever canine was commonly sighted in areas contaminated by Element a few centuries after my time, so it may be one of the few lifeforms to have survived the collapse of the ecosphere. Like the dogs of my day, this is a social animal that hunts smaller prey in packs.\r\nThat bony, scaled shell likely protects Armadoggo from radiation while also allowing it to burrow through the ground. It can cross long distances tunneling under the surface to avoid larger threats. It doesn’t seem threatened by us, and is in fact unusually curious about humans.\r\n\r\n\r\n家养\r\nArmadoggo seems happier once tamed and eager to help, much like its pampered cousins from my time. And it’s one fiercely protective pet, alerting you to nearby dangers and even keeping some at bay.\r\nArmadoggo turns out to have a knack for tracking down valuable technological trinkets hoarded by some of the corrupted local wildlife. Once it picks up the scent from an Element-poisoned kill, it will take you to its hoarded, eminently weaponizable treasure.\r\nNo leash training needed -- your loyal new companion will happily carry gear and armaments while never straying too far away. If your Armadoggo gets hurt, it’s smart enough to hide away underground where it can lick its wounds until it can rejoin you. Looking around at the mess we made of the world, I’m not sure we deserve their devotion.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
      //会挖地过来陪伴你
    },
