    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::1387102229",
      "Source": "Brute X-Spino",
      "Trans": {"SC":"凶恶X-棘龙","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::4045485069",
      "Source": "Corrupted Spino",
      "Trans": {"SC":"腐化棘龙","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":true,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::601202855",
      "Source": "Entry 4\nIf I'd ended up on this station instead of that island, I'd have never imagined the ecosystem was natural. Not for two seconds. \n\nTake these morellatops: they're a cross between a ceratops, a morelladon and a camel, and the strangest part? There are places in its humps where you can stick a spigot and get clean drinking water. Tastes like piss, but not only is it safe, it doesn't even harm the morellatops. It's crackers!\n\nDefinitely the result of genetic engineering, but I knew that, didn't I? It's time to get to the \"why.\" Maybe studying the creatures here with my new perspective will yield some insight.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"如果我最先到达的是焦土而不是孤岛, 我一定不会认为这里的生态系统是正常的, 一秒都不会。\n\n拿这些驼峰龙来说吧, 它们好像是角龙、棘龙和骆驼的混合体。最奇怪的是, 它们的驼峰上有些地方可以让你插一根龙头进去喝到新鲜的水。那水喝起来像尿, 不过这个水是无害的, 而且这么做根本不会伤到驼峰龙。真是疯狂。\n\n这绝对是是基因改造的结果, 不过我早就知道了, 不是吗? 现在该想想这是为什么了。也许研究这里的生物会为我带来一些新的发现。","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::1201636690",
      "Source": "Rockwell Recipes: Spinosaur Kibble",
      "Trans": {"SC":"罗克韦尔配方: 棘龙饲料","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::646774011",
      "Source": "Spinosaurus",
      "Trans": {"SC":"棘龙","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":true,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::300306639",
      "Source": "This recipe will produce a consumable which the Megalodon has a very high affinity for.\n\n1 Spinosaur Egg\n1 Prime Meat Jerky\n1 Savoroot\n2 Mejoberries\n3 Fiber (aids digestion)\nSubmerge in Water\nCook in a CookingPot",
      "Trans": {"SC":"这种食物深受巨齿鲨的喜爱。\n\n1颗棘龙蛋\n1份优质熟肉干\n1个土豆\n2个紫色浆果\n3个纤维 (帮助消化)\n加水没过\n在烹饪锅里烹调","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::2301216392",
      "Source": "X-Spino",
      "Trans": {"SC":"X-棘龙","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":true,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::3202815116",
      "Source": "Entry 3\nI'm on a roll. By sheer coincidence, I stumbled into another group of survivors today, and they didn't try to kill me or anything! If I didn't know how probability actually worked, I'd say that this recent string of good luck is the universe making up for sending me to the bloody desert in the first place.\n\nThe caravaners were welcoming, and the creatures they ride are fascinating. They seem like dinosaurs, but they also appear to share some biology with camels. Bizarre! For all its oddities, the island never had anything like that.\n\nI'll have to study them...after a nap. All this desert survival's left me knackered.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"我真是好运不断。在机缘巧合之下, 我撞见了另外一群生存者, 而且他们并没有试图杀了我或是对我做别的什么。如果不是我撞大运了, 那么就是上天为了补偿将我扔到这个该死的沙漠中。\n\n这个旅行队的人很好客, 而且他们骑得生物很迷人。它们看起来像恐龙, 但是它们又好像和骆驼有什么生物学上的关系 (驼峰龙)。太奇怪了! 我在孤岛上从没有见过任何像它们的生物。\n\n我必须研究它们...不过我先要睡一觉。沙漠求生让我筋疲力尽。","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::1592863384",
      "Source": "I'm definitely more prepared for this desert than before, and better equipped. With my morellatops offering a large, mobile supply of water and Radar looking out for the weather, the only threat I really have to worry about is major predators. Also giant golems.\n\nI'm actually impressed with the shape I'm in, if I do say so myself. I think I even saw some ab definition the other day! Took me long enough. I've been living without sweets for ages, after all, you'd think I'd get fit much quicker. \n\nGreat, now I miss sweets. The things I'd do to taste chocolate again...",
      "Trans": {"SC":"相较于之前, 我对于沙漠旅行的准备更加充分了, 而且装备也更好了。我的驼峰龙提供了大量的可移动水源, 而雷达会预报天气, 我唯一需要担心的就是大型食肉动物。还有岩石巨人。\n\n要我自己评价的话, 我对我自己现在的状态感觉很好。我已经很久没有吃过糖了, 不然我很快就会发胖了。\n\n好极了, 现在我开始想念糖了。为了吃巧克力我会豁出去的...","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::1510035080",
      "Source": "Just who or what Wali al Aswad is depends on who you ask. Some of the villagers have attached a religious connotation to the figure, believing it to be some sort of heavenly guardian who appears to the worthy in their time of need. One villager is even convinced Wali is an extraterrestrial.\n\nI don't deal in beliefs. I deal in empirical evidence, and that means nothing about Wali is certain until I can meet them. I won't forget this village's kindness, especially after granting me a morellatops and supplies for my journey, but this is why I'm here – to find answers.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"瓦力·阿尔·奥斯瓦德是谁或者什么东西, 每个人的回答都不一样。有的村民把这个人和宗教信仰搭上了关系, 认为他是一名来自上天的守护神, 在需要的时候才会出现。一名村民甚至深信瓦力是一个外星人。\n\n我不接受信仰。我只接受事实证据, 这表明在我见到瓦力之前, 一切都是不确定的。我不会忘记村民的善意, 尤其是在他们送给我一头驼峰龙和旅途所需的补给品之后, 但这就是我来这里的原因 -- 寻找答案。","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::2244923478",
      "Source": "Molleratops",
      "Trans": {"SC":"驼峰龙","JA":"駝峰龙"},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::44684665",
      "Source": "Of course Wali lives on a bloody mountain. Of course they do. I saw their wyverns land at the summit yesterday, and they haven't left. This has to be their home...unfortunately.\n\nThe paths were too narrow for my morellatops, so I had to leave it behind. It should know to wander off if I don't return for it, not that I can really afford to worry about it. The climb's doing a fine job of kicking my ass even without distractions.\n\nI swear, if I don't have a six pack after climbing a mountain in the bloody desert, I'm going to be awfully cross. ",
      "Trans": {"SC":"瓦力当然住在一座该死的山上了! 当然了! 我昨天看到飞龙降落在一座山峰上, 并且没有离开。不幸的是...这一定是它们的家了。\n\n上山的道路对我的饿驼峰龙而言太狭窄了, 所以我不得不把它留在原地。如果我回不来的话, 它应该会自己走开的, 对此我倒不是很担心。哪怕没有别的什么东西让我分心, 爬山真的把我折腾得死去活来。\n\n我发誓, 如果我发现自己爬上沙漠里的一座山峰后没有练出六块腹肌来, 我一定会发飙的。","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::3757957258",
      "Source": "Today, I caught a glimpse of what the caravaners call the \"Endless Dunes\" – the desolate sea of sand that apparently surrounds the livable portion of the desert on all sides. \n\nSurely these dunes must end, but it's easy to see why one might believe otherwise. Not only do they stretch on to the horizon, which I now know must actually be some kind of holographic projection, but they're home to – get this – giant sand \"worms\" that will devour anything that sets foot in their domain.\n\nI laughed that off at first. Then I saw a creature the size of a train burst forth from the sand and devour a wild morellatops that had wandered into its territory. I suppose I'll just have to learn to walk without rhythm...",
      "Trans": {"SC":"今天我看到了被旅行队称为“无尽沙丘”的地方。这片无际的沙海似乎从四周包围了这片沙漠中可以居住的地方。\n\n当然啦, 这片沙丘不可能这的是无尽的, 不过很容易可以看出人们为什么这么称呼它。这片沙丘不仅绵延万里, 而且这里还是这些...这些巨大的“沙虫” (死亡蠕虫) 的家园。它们会吞噬任何踏足它们领土的东西。\n\n一开始我还对这些说法嗤之以鼻, 直到我看到了一个如同火车般大小的生物从沙子里冲出来, 吞噬了一头误入它领土的野生驼峰龙。我想我以后走路要非常小心了...","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
